<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xsd:schema xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
	xmlns="http://ei/core/address"
	targetNamespace="http://ei/core/address">
	<xsd:complexType name="AddressType">
		<xsd:annotation>
			<xsd:documentation>
This business object contains address elements.
		</xsd:documentation>
		</xsd:annotation>
		<xsd:sequence>
			<xsd:element name="AddressLine1" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is the first line of an address.
				</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="AddressLine2" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is the second line of an address.
				</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="CityName" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is the city of an address.
				</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="StateOrProvinceCode" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is a code for a state, province or territory within a country or nation.
The E1T00111 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
 				</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="StateOrProvinceName" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is the name for a state, province or territory within a country or nation.
The E1T00111 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
  			</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="StateOrProvinceAbbreviation"
				type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is the abbreviation for a state, province or territory within a country or nation.
The E1T00111 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
			</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="PostalCode" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element identifies a specific postal location. 
				</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="CountryCode" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is a code for a country, nation or political state.
The E1T00101 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
				</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="CountryName" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is the name for a country, nation or political state.
The E1T00101 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
				</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element name="CountryAbbreviation" type="xsd:string"
				minOccurs="0">
				<xsd:annotation>
					<xsd:documentation>
This element is the abbreviation for a country, nation or political state.
The E1T00101 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
			</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="ISOCountryCode"
				type="xsd:string"><xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>This element is the abbreviation used by the International Standards Organization (ISO) that identifies a country, nation or political state.
The E1T00101 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element in the &quot;ISO_CNTRY_C&quot; column. </xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
		</xsd:sequence>
	</xsd:complexType>
	<xsd:element name="Address" type="AddressType" />
</xsd:schema>
